 ```
 
 
+Rotate a queue in place. Positive steps move items from the back to the front;
+negative steps move items from the front to the back. The method returns the
+same queue and normalizes integer counts by the current length:
+
+```js
+const denque = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+denque.rotate(); // [4, 1, 2, 3]
+denque.rotate(-1); // [1, 2, 3, 4]
+```
+
+`rotate` throws an `Error` for non-number, non-integer, or non-finite counts.
+
 See the [API reference documentation](https://docs.page/invertase/denque/api) for more examples.
 
